WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.790
Bloodshot has one of the best mid-movie twists
of any superhero flick, but that big reveal

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.680
comes at a cost.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:10.200
There simply isn't enough time in Bloodshot's
short runtime to explain what's real, what's

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.980
not, and how everything fits together.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.000
We'd really, really like some of these answers.

00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:18.500
It's impossible to talk about Bloodshot without
giving away the big twist: Nothing that Ray

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.980
Garrison remembers about his past is real.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.730
His daring hostage rescue?

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.040
His luxurious Italian vacation with his beautiful
wife, Gina?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.230
Their murder at the hands of a crazed terrorist?

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.390
All fabrications of Rising Spirit Technologies,
the military contractor that's been wiping

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:36.539
away Ray's memories and replacing them with
fantasies designed to make him the ultimate

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.180
weapon.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.300
So, then, who is Ray?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.800
Bloodshot looks like it's going to tell us
when Ray tracks down Gina, but doesn't actually

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.120
give us any answers.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.400
From what Gina says, we can infer that Ray
really was a member of the military, and really

00:00:47.409 --> 00:00:49.409
did go on highly classified missions.

00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:53.699
His name actually is Ray, and his relationship
with Gina ended five years before the movie

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:54.699
takes place.

00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:55.699
That's all we really know.

00:00:55.699 --> 00:00:57.610
"You know nothing about men like me."

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:58.610
You said it, Ray.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:02.460
Given how much of the movie seems to hinge
on Bloodshot's mistaken identity, it's strange

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.560
that we didn't get any answers to this question
at all.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.740
RST's nanites are miraculous in many ways.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.270
Not only do they give their owner superpowers,
but if you believe RST founder and lead scientist

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.310
Emil Harting, they also bring people back
from the dead.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.310
But is that true?

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.920
As we've seen, it's hard to take Dr. Harting
at his word, and Ray's death is a fake memory.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.700
Not only is Ray's real cause of death left
unexplained, but it's not even clear that

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.450
he actually died in the first place.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.400
For example, Gina is surprised to see Ray
when he shows up unannounced at her door,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.979
but she's not that surprised.

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:36.659
It's the kind of shock that comes from running
into a former lover unexpectedly, not from

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:39.320
seeing a dead ex-boyfriend suddenly risen
from the grave.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.860
If Ray had passed away, you'd expect that
Gina would've at least heard about it ... they're

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.720
not together any more, but they clearly still
care about each other ... unless RST covered

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.280
it up.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.820
And if they did, then we're back to the original
question: What happened that needed to be

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.120
kept under wraps?

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.299
Bloodshot isn't actually hunting terrorists.

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:59.610
He's tracking down and killing former RST
employees, who Dr. Harting fears will spill

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.360
the company's secrets to competitors.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.430
What we don't know, however, is why all of
these people left their presumably high-paying

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.060
jobs doing cutting-edge research in the first
place.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.360
And for that matter, why did Harting let everyone
go in the first place?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.170
When KT tries to defect, Harting turns off
her implant, making it impossible to leave.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.730
Harting clearly isn't above using violence
to keep his employees in line ... why didn't

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.340
he stop the problem before it started, rather
than force a supersoldier to clean up his

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.020
mess later?

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.780
By the end of the film, RST's servers have
been blown to pieces, its CEO and former executives

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.440
are all dead, and its corporate headquarters
are in shambles.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.211
For all intents and purposes, it's done and
gone.

00:02:35.211 --> 00:02:37.400
It also collapsed in a fairly public fashion,
too.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.520
A superhero brawl doesn't happen on a busy
city street without anyone noticing.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.269
There's bound to be some cellphone footage
of the fight out there.

00:02:44.269 --> 00:02:45.909
Even Justice League got that right.

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:48.940
In the past, this is the sort of thing that
RST would've covered up.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.940
Now, though?

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.560
There's nothing stopping an in-depth investigation
from happening, or keeping a lid on the fact

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.910
that a military contractor has created superheroes,
who now walk among us.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.720
Repercussions seem inevitable, but Bloodshot
doesn't offer any clues as to how they'll

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.300
play out.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.980
Gina DeCarlo still cares about Ray Garrison,
but she's no longer in love with him.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.599
Gina makes that very, very clear when Ray
shows up on her doorstep, looking for answers,

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:15.030
and she dismisses him with a simple but telling
phrase: "I have a family."

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:18.409
That being said, Gina seems to have gotten
that family awfully quickly.

00:03:18.409 --> 00:03:22.299
She broke up with Ray five years ago, but
that's a very quick time to get over a major

00:03:22.299 --> 00:03:26.720
relationship, start a new one, get married,
and have at least two children, one of whom

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.300
looks like she's at least four years old.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.659
Besides that, Ray shares one long, meaningful
look with Gina's daughter that implies there's

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:34.920
a little more to this story than Gina is letting
on.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.920
That glance stands out because it's such a
weird, awkward moment.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.620
And besides, why don't we see Gina's other
kid, or meet her husband?

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:45.020
Everything in the way the scene is shot seems
to imply that one, if not both, of the kids

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.020
are Ray's.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.540
At the same time, there's no real evidence
in either the dialogue or the story to support

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.080
the theory that Ray is secretly the child's
father.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.540
Is that just the product of some odd editing
choices, or is there something more going

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.100
on?

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.910
Emil Harting lies about everything.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.150
He just can't stop himself.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.790
Obviously, for his scheme to work, some fibs
are necessary.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.200
Ray needs to believe that his wife was murdered,
and that a former RST employee pulled the

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:06.820
trigger.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.000
However, that doesn't explain everything.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:13.260
When rebooting Bloodshot, it sounds like Emil
changes small details in Bloodshot's origin

00:04:13.269 --> 00:04:14.470
story just for fun.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.220
"And we're gonna put this memory in your head
and we're going to weaponize you.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.500
We're gonna get you to do what we want you
to do, because we can."

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:21.970
Take Harting's backstory, for example.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:25.940
When we first meet Harting, the not-so-good
doctor says that he was a childhood tennis

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.320
prodigy who then lost his arm to cancer.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.789
The second time, however, Harting decides
to tell Ray he played cricket.

00:04:31.789 --> 00:04:36.380
Not only is that strange but it raises another
question: Is any part of Harting's story true,

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.940
and if not, what really happened to his arm?

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.220
"Did you ever figure out what happened to
your arm?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:41.480
Nope."

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:47.200
In fact, if Harting is lying about his own
injury, who's to say that Tibbs and Dalton's

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:47.780
histories are any more accurate?

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.160
Were they even soldiers?

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.610
Not that it matters too much ... they're all
dead either way ... but it's certainly something

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:53.140
to think about.

